WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.523
[RAIN PATTERING]


00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:11.446
[ELECTRICAL BUZZING]


00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:17.160
[BUZZING CEASES]


00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:24.292
[WIND HOWLING]


00:01:25.376 --> 00:01:27.754
[VEHICLE CREAKING]


00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:33.134
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]


00:02:09.754 --> 00:02:11.631
CRICKET: "...the last rains
came gently,


00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:16.177
"and they did not cut
the scarred earth.


00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:19.556
"The plows crossed
and recrossed
the rivulet marks.


00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.893
"The last rains
lifted the corn quickly


00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:28.356
"and scattered
weed colonies and grass
along the sides of the roads


00:02:28.398 --> 00:02:29.816
"so that the gray country


00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:31.693
"and the dark red country
began to disappear..."


00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.862
[THUNDER RUMBLING]


00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:40.743
[THUNDER RUMBLING]


00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:44.205
AUGUSTUS:  You listened to
the sermon today?


00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.415
OSCAR: Yes, sir.


00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:47.709
AUGUSTUS: And?


00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.252
OSCAR: I don't know.


00:02:49.294 --> 00:02:52.255
AUGUSTUS: I don't know?
[CHUCKLES]


00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:54.215
"I don't know," is not
much of an answer, boy.


00:02:55.884 --> 00:02:58.553
Ah, pulled in nap time.


00:02:58.595 --> 00:03:01.347
I don't care much
for the Reverend's rhetoric.


00:03:01.764 --> 00:03:03.850
In fact, I'm sure his papi,


00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:05.435
Reverend senior would be
rolling in his grave


00:03:05.476 --> 00:03:07.562
for some of the utterings
coming out of his mouth


00:03:07.604 --> 00:03:08.771
in the house of the Lord.


00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.858
But I think we both understand


00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.902
what he was
basically getting at.


00:03:14.777 --> 00:03:15.904
I think so.


00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:21.409
You see, Oscar,


00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:24.412
there comes a time
when a man's gotta
step up, son.


00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:29.626
Not so much for himself,


00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.586
but for the betterment
of others.


00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:33.254
You understand what I mean?


00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:36.633
And when that time comes,


00:03:36.674 --> 00:03:40.428
we as men,
we have to be ready
to oblige it.


00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.603
[THUNDER RUMBLING]


00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:58.780
[RAILWAY BELL RINGING]


00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:03.785
-It's a mighty fine meal, Jo.
-Thank you.


00:04:03.826 --> 00:04:05.828
-OSCAR: Thanks, Mom.
-You're welcome, honey.


00:04:10.541 --> 00:04:13.586
Oscar, you're gonna
run this over to Loux?


00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:17.423
Josephine, do not be
giving away what's ours.


00:04:17.465 --> 00:04:19.425
Augustus, those children
won't eat otherwise.


00:04:21.678 --> 00:04:22.971
JOSEPHINE: Take this to them
and hurry home.


00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:24.013
[WHISPERING] Yeah.


00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:26.307
Come over here, boy.


00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.310
Don't be lagging.


00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:32.480
I don't want you catching
whatever virus lingers
in that house, all right?


00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:34.983
Yes, sir.


00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.538
[KNOCK AT THE DOOR]


00:04:48.579 --> 00:04:49.706
[WOMAN ON TV
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:51.541
It's open.


00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.046
-LOUX: Hey, Oscar.
-OSCAR: Hey.


00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:02.552
PERSEY: Hey, dove.


00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:04.012
What you got there?


00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:05.680
It's chop from my mum.


00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:11.394
-Loux, why don't you go
crank up the stove?
-All right.


00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:13.062
-PERSEY: Take your brother
in there.
-LOUX: Amos.


00:05:18.776 --> 00:05:21.029
Boy.


00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:24.032
Did you not hear me?
Get your ass in there
and help your sister.


00:05:27.744 --> 00:05:28.870
-[YELLING]
Get your ass in there!
-[YELLING] Hey!


00:05:28.911 --> 00:05:29.912
[AMOS GASPS]


00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.042
Huh?


00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:38.921
[PERSEY LAUGHING]


00:05:38.963 --> 00:05:42.050
Hey! You're a daft
little fucker, ain't you?


00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:44.886
[PERSEY LAUGHS]


00:05:50.725 --> 00:05:52.518
[SNIFFLES, SIGHS]


00:05:55.438 --> 00:05:56.439
Oscar.


00:05:58.608 --> 00:05:59.609
Come here, boy.


00:06:00.443 --> 00:06:01.611
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]


00:06:03.946 --> 00:06:06.741
Why don't you do something
for me now?


00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:10.078
I want you to tell
that daddy of yours
I don't need his givings.


00:06:10.119 --> 00:06:13.956
I don't need his
nor your mom's
backhanded charity.


00:06:13.998 --> 00:06:15.124
You understand me?


00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:20.046
Loux, cut the stove off,
give the feast back
to Oscar.


00:06:20.088 --> 00:06:22.090
-LOUX: But, Dad...
-Just do it, baby.


00:06:22.423 --> 00:06:24.467
PERSEY: You heard me.


00:06:24.509 --> 00:06:25.927
LOUX: But... [SIGHS]


00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:26.969
PERSEY: Do what I say.


00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:39.732
Here, take it back.


00:06:41.943 --> 00:06:43.069
Get the fuck out of my house.


00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.491
[YELLING] Go!


00:06:52.537 --> 00:06:55.998
[WOMAN ON TV
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:07:33.578 --> 00:07:37.123
[PERSEY SNORING]


00:07:42.753 --> 00:07:45.840
[PERSEY SNORING]


00:07:47.758 --> 00:07:49.051
[WHISPERING] Loux?


00:07:50.928 --> 00:07:52.013
[WHISPERING] Loux!


00:07:52.763 --> 00:07:53.806
Amos?


00:07:58.269 --> 00:08:02.190
[PERSEY SNORING]


00:08:21.918 --> 00:08:25.755
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]


00:08:28.966 --> 00:08:30.843
-OSCAR: You okay?
-LOUX: Yeah.


00:08:33.971 --> 00:08:35.056
OSCAR: What happened?


00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:37.934
PERSEY: Come sit with me.


00:08:40.603 --> 00:08:42.271
Get in there. [SNIFFLES]


00:08:43.272 --> 00:08:44.565
Mmm.


00:08:45.983 --> 00:08:47.610
[IMITATING BEAR SOUNDS]


00:08:47.652 --> 00:08:48.903
[CHUCKLES]


00:08:48.945 --> 00:08:50.571
[IMITATING BEAR SOUNDS]


00:08:50.613 --> 00:08:52.907
[PERSEY LAUGHS]


00:08:53.449 --> 00:08:55.701
[SNIFFLES] You know
I love you, right?


00:08:59.121 --> 00:09:01.082
-Will you love me?
-Mmm-hmm.


00:09:05.795 --> 00:09:07.255
No one will ever hurt you.


00:09:10.007 --> 00:09:12.260
You getting to be real pretty,
you know that?


00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.805
I didn't notice
how much you've grown up.


00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:22.270
[KISSING]


00:09:23.646 --> 00:09:24.814
LOUX: I couldn't stop him.


00:09:26.649 --> 00:09:27.900
OSCAR: You have to
do something.


00:09:28.693 --> 00:09:29.777
LOUX: What do you mean?


00:09:30.861 --> 00:09:32.280
There's nowhere else
for us to go.


00:09:33.656 --> 00:09:34.657
OSCAR: You could live
out here.


00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.995
No one telling you what to do.


00:09:45.334 --> 00:09:46.335
[OSCAR WHISPERING]
Can you hear them?


00:09:48.045 --> 00:09:49.130
They're in the wind.


00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.633
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]


00:09:52.675 --> 00:09:54.093
Their screams.


00:09:55.177 --> 00:09:57.096
They were here long before us.


00:09:58.222 --> 00:10:00.808
And they will be forever.


00:10:02.685 --> 00:10:04.312
-[EXCLAIMS SUDDENLY]
-[LOUX SCOFFS]


00:10:04.353 --> 00:10:07.648
-[AMOS BREATHING HEAVILY]
-LOUX: It's okay.


00:10:08.357 --> 00:10:09.775
It's okay.


00:10:09.817 --> 00:10:11.110
[BLOWING]


00:10:11.152 --> 00:10:13.863
[FIRE CRACKLING]


00:10:20.036 --> 00:10:22.163
[INDISTINCT SOUNDS ON TV]


00:10:35.259 --> 00:10:38.054
[PERSEY EXHALES]


00:10:48.272 --> 00:10:50.858
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]


00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:05.206
[DOOR CREAKING]


00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.875
[SNORING]


00:11:32.274 --> 00:11:34.777
[FIRE CRACKLING]


00:11:39.115 --> 00:11:41.784
[MUSIC INTENSIFIES]


00:12:06.016 --> 00:12:09.145
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]


00:12:41.844 --> 00:12:44.305
[]


00:13:25.221 --> 00:13:26.847
[HORN HONKING]


00:13:32.102 --> 00:13:35.064
[]


00:14:14.478 --> 00:14:17.439
LOUX:  I have been wanting
to give you this.


00:14:17.481 --> 00:14:20.442
It was my mom's.
My dad won't let me wear it.


00:14:20.734 --> 00:14:22.236
I want you to have it.


00:14:24.488 --> 00:14:25.573
Let me help you.


00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:32.121
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]


00:14:55.144 --> 00:14:56.270
[LOCK CLICKS OPEN]


00:15:07.448 --> 00:15:08.991
Got another minor, Keryn.


00:15:11.535 --> 00:15:13.954
Look at you.
You're just a baby.


00:15:17.166 --> 00:15:18.459
We're short-staffed tonight.


00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:19.627
[TELEPHONE RINGING]


00:15:19.668 --> 00:15:21.337
That's fine.
I'll take him to Six.


00:15:21.587 --> 00:15:23.130
Come on, boy.


00:15:23.172 --> 00:15:25.341
[INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
ON PA]


00:15:26.383 --> 00:15:27.468
[DOOR SLAMS SHUT]


00:15:44.193 --> 00:15:46.028
[TELEPHONE RINGING]


00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.034
[INTERNET DIAL-UP TONE]


00:15:55.037 --> 00:15:56.705
[FAX MACHINE RINGING]


00:15:58.374 --> 00:16:00.334
[FAX MACHINE WHIRRING]


00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.553
I got another one for you.


00:16:14.682 --> 00:16:16.350
Is that the boy
who came in last night?


00:16:20.062 --> 00:16:22.648
Does that kid look like
a murderer to you, Keryn?


00:16:23.524 --> 00:16:26.068
No, he doesn't.


00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.487
Says this one's from
out near the marsh too.


00:16:28.529 --> 00:16:32.324
How is a kid gonna get
a hundred miles away overnight?


00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.703
Think he's got accomplices?


00:16:35.744 --> 00:16:38.330
You think
there's a conspiracy here?


00:16:38.372 --> 00:16:40.249
-[LAUGHS]
-I don't know.


00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.418
They're all starting to look
the same to me.


00:16:42.459 --> 00:16:43.711
I'll leave you to it.


00:16:49.466 --> 00:16:50.759
[GATE UNLOCKING]


00:16:50.801 --> 00:16:54.555
-[LOCK CLICKS OPEN]
-[DOOR CREAKING]


00:16:54.596 --> 00:16:56.056
-FLANNERY: Boy.
-[GASPS]


00:16:59.435 --> 00:17:00.602
Go on.


00:17:53.155 --> 00:17:54.073
GIRL: "Oscar,


00:17:54.114 --> 00:17:58.285
"Clean up after yourself
and put the milk delivery away.
We'll see you tonight.


00:17:58.786 --> 00:18:00.120
"Love, Mom."


00:18:02.873 --> 00:18:04.291
I'm Peaches.


00:18:07.377 --> 00:18:08.420
You hungry?


00:18:10.172 --> 00:18:11.173
Go ahead.


00:18:18.388 --> 00:18:19.473
Come on.


00:18:19.515 --> 00:18:21.600
Don't worry. Come on.


00:18:33.695 --> 00:18:36.323
OSCAR: Where are your parents?


00:18:36.365 --> 00:18:39.201
My mom died when I was three.
I never knew my father.


00:18:42.538 --> 00:18:45.332
I have a place to live,
people who look out for me.


00:18:53.841 --> 00:18:56.343
Now, the real question is
where do you live?


00:19:05.936 --> 00:19:07.855
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]


00:19:14.945 --> 00:19:16.196
PEACHES: Watch your step.


00:19:28.417 --> 00:19:29.418
After you.


00:19:45.976 --> 00:19:48.270
COTTON: Well, look who it is.


00:19:49.438 --> 00:19:50.939
Took her forever to get back.


00:19:50.981 --> 00:19:52.566
Thought she tried to
run away again like last time.


00:19:53.817 --> 00:19:57.446
Fellas, this is Oscar.


00:19:57.487 --> 00:19:59.948
Oscar, this is my family
of broken toys.


00:20:14.963 --> 00:20:15.964
Sway?


00:20:17.799 --> 00:20:18.800
Sway!


00:20:20.677 --> 00:20:21.720
Come in.


00:20:27.976 --> 00:20:31.271
No. No. No!


00:20:31.313 --> 00:20:32.981
No room for him.


00:20:33.023 --> 00:20:34.733
Sway, come on.
He's got nowhere to go.


00:20:34.775 --> 00:20:35.776
Said no.


00:20:37.694 --> 00:20:39.279
God, will you please
just take a look?


00:20:39.321 --> 00:20:40.447
I found him
outside the station.


00:20:40.489 --> 00:20:41.990
Quit being so fucking lazy.


00:20:43.325 --> 00:20:44.993
Oh, listen to the lady.


00:20:48.705 --> 00:20:50.624
Now let me have a look at you.


00:20:54.044 --> 00:20:56.964
I'm gentle as a lamb's ear.


00:20:57.005 --> 00:20:58.590
[SWAY EXHALES]


00:21:02.052 --> 00:21:03.428
PEACHES: His name is Oscar.


00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.348
Ah, I see.


00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:11.311
Do you know
what your name means, boy?


00:21:12.562 --> 00:21:13.689
No.


00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:15.857
Oscar, uh,


00:21:15.899 --> 00:21:19.695
divine spear,
champion warrior.


00:21:19.736 --> 00:21:21.530
[TRAIN WHIRRING PAST]


00:21:21.571 --> 00:21:22.864
[INDISTINCT]


00:21:27.577 --> 00:21:29.454
You are a champion,
aren't you?


00:21:30.539 --> 00:21:31.957
Huh?


00:21:31.999 --> 00:21:34.334
Noble. [GRUNTS]


00:21:35.043 --> 00:21:36.795
[INHALES DEEPLY]


00:21:36.837 --> 00:21:40.966
You've made decisions
only a man should make,
not a boy.


00:21:44.594 --> 00:21:47.347
Should be a natural. [EXHALES]


00:21:55.439 --> 00:21:56.732
[BELL JINGLING]


00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:00.027
Billy.


00:22:05.907 --> 00:22:09.411
Uh... I know, I know.


00:22:09.453 --> 00:22:11.038
BIRDIE: You know
what, Neville?


00:22:11.747 --> 00:22:12.873
Not to come here.


00:22:14.583 --> 00:22:15.917
But I do understand, you know,


00:22:15.959 --> 00:22:19.838
you liking the ambience
and all, so...


00:22:21.089 --> 00:22:22.883
-Neville.
-What?


00:22:25.093 --> 00:22:27.596
Right. Well, it's about
the new boy.


00:22:28.805 --> 00:22:29.890
BIRDIE: All right.


00:22:29.931 --> 00:22:31.933
Well, you just
bring him by the office.


00:22:33.643 --> 00:22:34.853
SWAY: He has family.


00:22:36.146 --> 00:22:37.898
He ain't told me
where he's from,


00:22:37.939 --> 00:22:39.066
but he's not from the city.


00:22:39.816 --> 00:22:42.027
So... You know,


00:22:42.069 --> 00:22:44.905
I mean, I was thinking that
we don't have the room.


00:22:44.946 --> 00:22:50.577
You see, this is why
I leave the selection process
to Flan.


00:22:50.619 --> 00:22:53.455
If this was your show,
we'd be running
a goddamn petting zoo.


00:22:54.289 --> 00:22:56.041
I was just thinking that--


00:22:56.083 --> 00:22:57.626
Well, don't be
thinking, Neville.


00:22:57.667 --> 00:22:59.586
It ain't what
you do good, okay?


00:23:04.132 --> 00:23:06.635
Look... Do you want to
meet him?


00:23:11.765 --> 00:23:13.141
-You brought him here?
-Yeah, I did.


00:23:13.183 --> 00:23:15.060
Oh, Jesus Christ.


00:23:15.102 --> 00:23:16.436
What? I just...


00:23:16.478 --> 00:23:18.647
Well... [SIGHS]


00:23:18.688 --> 00:23:20.982
All right, look,
I'll go get him.


00:23:25.987 --> 00:23:27.948
[BELL JINGLING]


00:23:27.989 --> 00:23:29.491
SWAY: Come here, come here.
Come on.


00:23:39.668 --> 00:23:41.002
BIRDIE: They treatin' you
all right?


00:23:41.044 --> 00:23:43.505
-Go ahead, answer him.
-[NERVOUSLY] Yes, sir.


00:23:46.883 --> 00:23:47.968
Good.


00:23:49.511 --> 00:23:51.179
You just keep your eyes open.


00:23:51.221 --> 00:23:52.848
Maybe you'll learn
a thing or two.


00:23:56.017 --> 00:23:57.978
Okay, all right. Okay.


00:23:58.019 --> 00:23:59.020
Go on out.


00:24:01.565 --> 00:24:02.649
[BIRDIE CHUCKLES]


00:24:04.192 --> 00:24:07.028
I like him. Oh, he stays.


00:24:08.738 --> 00:24:10.157
[WHISPERING] Goddamnit.


00:24:14.744 --> 00:24:15.996
[WHISPERING] Goddamnit!


00:24:19.082 --> 00:24:20.500
How's the ticker, Neville?


00:24:23.712 --> 00:24:25.172
Running like a Swiss watch.


00:24:30.760 --> 00:24:31.803
Billy.


00:24:39.060 --> 00:24:41.062
[SIGHS]


00:24:41.938 --> 00:24:45.859
["OUT IN THE WOODS" PLAYING]


00:24:51.781 --> 00:24:54.242
SWAY: Go! You know what to do.


00:24:55.243 --> 00:24:59.080
Going down a hard road


00:24:59.122 --> 00:25:00.207
And you?


00:25:00.248 --> 00:25:01.541
Just don't know


00:25:01.583 --> 00:25:05.837
Don't know where I've been


00:25:05.879 --> 00:25:08.590
So what we provide here
is an education.


00:25:09.966 --> 00:25:11.259
A way of life.


00:25:13.261 --> 00:25:15.055
Fit only for wolves.


00:25:16.139 --> 00:25:19.267
Sir... [INDISTINCT]


00:25:19.309 --> 00:25:21.603
Oh, yeah, down there and...


00:25:21.645 --> 00:25:25.232
SWAY:  And me,
I'm the headmaster,
or the conductor.


00:25:25.273 --> 00:25:26.733
Bloop!


00:25:28.944 --> 00:25:30.028
Look around.


00:25:30.820 --> 00:25:31.905
What do you see?


00:25:31.947 --> 00:25:34.950
People make me crazy


00:25:34.991 --> 00:25:36.618
Simple-minded people.


00:25:38.620 --> 00:25:39.788
Cogs in the wheel.


00:25:41.665 --> 00:25:44.960
Television, magazines,
billboards.


00:25:45.001 --> 00:25:46.127
Other people's dreams.


00:25:48.797 --> 00:25:53.760
They've been told how to look,
think, feel.


00:25:53.802 --> 00:25:55.929
They've never had
an original thought.


00:25:59.349 --> 00:26:01.309
You know what separates us
from them?


00:26:04.354 --> 00:26:06.815
The gift of desperation.


00:26:11.152 --> 00:26:12.153
Whoa


